    "SLG_Legion_Presence": "Legion Presence",
    "SLG_Legion_Presence_desc": "The Spanish Legion was sent in to protect its Portuguese brothers as they resettled into the land. Most importantly, however, they were deployed to govern the territory in the absence of French authority. It remains the predominant political and military force in the area, and controls much of what happens in the region...",
    "SLG_Retornados": "Portuguese Retornados",
    "SLG_Retornados_desc": "In the wake of the German invasion of Portuguese Africa, many of our citizens chose to return to Iberian territory. Thus, the government decided to place them in the unofficially Iberian-controlled region of Algeria as part of a scheme to reinforce their claims over the territory. To this day, Portuguese settlers inhabit the territory, providing us a base to work towards a stronger nation.",
    "SLG_Native_Unrest": "Native Unrest",
    "SLG_Native_Unrest_desc": "The establishment of military governorates over Algeria was not a decision made out of idle ambition, but one Rome and Madrid would claim to have been a necessity.\n\nAlgeria has become a boiling cauldron verging on a detonation that would threaten both of its neighboring Empires. In spite of their bitter rejection of the fact, no amount of troops, equipment nor populist measures that either force can muster can change Algeria's present state of affairs. All Rome and Madrid can achieve is delaying the inevitable and squabbling over which is more worthy to inherit the ashes.",
